    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.97 from 6 h onward, which could mean the reader is saturated. I tested this by diluting the 18 h aliquot. Readings scaled back by the dilution factor were 0.995 at 3x, 1.064 at 10x and 0.936 at 40x. The undiluted reading was 0.972. These all agree within noise, and there is no systematic rise with dilution, which saturation would produce. The reader is therefore responding linearly at OD ≈ 1. The culture really is in stationary phase at about 1.0, and the biomass is as the undiluted readings indicate."
